****
While neutral metal lines show plages as somewhat brighter, ionized metals darken them. 
Flares aside, everything is shades of darker on the disk. 

With continuum subtraction, prominences are revealed as fainter instances of what is visible in hydrogen alpha. 

When compared to nearby neutral lines, also showing prominences, like in the case of the Mg b triplet, with Fe II,
pay attention to the prominences' Doppler shifts.

The above images have had their contrast enhanced via continuum subtraction. 
In the Atlas, scrolling through the cubes and tuning into these wavelengths, one can see that the signal is there,
and its strength varies from line to line, being particularly strong in Fe II 5018 for example.
